WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:44.963
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:45.233 --> 00:46.568
There are more than 200,000 men…

3
00:47.944 --> 00:48.945
And the Toyotomi?

4
00:50.280 --> 00:51.364
73,000.

5
00:58.037 --> 00:59.038
Are you all right?

6
00:59.122 --> 00:59.956
Yeah.

7
01:00.665 --> 01:02.167
Make sure you take care of yourself.

8
01:03.334 --> 01:05.837
I really want you to open that restaurant someday, Seikai.

9
01:06.838 --> 01:09.841
Well, I want you to make your dream come true too, brother.

10
01:10.967 --> 01:14.262
SECRET TALKS - TAISEIJI TEMPLE

11
01:25.273 --> 01:27.400
Hey… you lot.

12
01:29.736 --> 01:31.070
What have you done to them?

13
01:31.738 --> 01:32.739
Hey!

14
01:33.531 --> 01:34.365
Release me!

15
01:34.949 --> 01:36.659
Get these damn things off!

16
01:37.744 --> 01:39.120
Don't just stand there!

17
01:40.830 --> 01:41.664
You bastard!

18
01:45.043 --> 01:46.669
Hattori Hanzo…

19
01:47.545 --> 01:49.297
You'll pay for what you did to the old man.

20
01:50.757 --> 01:52.050
I'll kill you!

21
01:52.133 --> 01:53.760
You know this one, Hanzo?

22
01:53.843 --> 01:55.970
He was the ninja under Hakuunsai.

23
01:57.013 --> 01:59.307
So this is the one you failed to kill.

24
02:02.310 --> 02:03.228
Magnificent.

25
02:04.646 --> 02:06.105
So you're Ieyasu.

26
02:07.398 --> 02:09.776
A ninja who can leap across a river 30 ken wide.

27
02:10.360 --> 02:12.987
With the right training, he could leap even farther.

28
02:14.155 --> 02:15.114
All the better,

29
02:16.032 --> 02:17.992
since our beast has yet to awaken.

30
02:18.952 --> 02:20.578
-What? -Ninja.

31
02:21.496 --> 02:22.789
Come serve me.

32
02:23.915 --> 02:26.542
I don't take orders from anyone!

33
02:27.168 --> 02:28.878
I'll give you whatever your heart desires.

34
02:29.796 --> 02:30.880
What do you want?

35
02:31.839 --> 02:32.757
Money?

36
02:33.967 --> 02:34.926
Women?

37
02:35.927 --> 02:38.346
The Ogosho himself is offering you a place in his service.

38
02:39.514 --> 02:40.390
Hey.

39
02:41.099 --> 02:43.184
There could be no greater honor.

40
02:45.937 --> 02:47.021
Who the hell are you?

41
02:47.814 --> 02:49.691
Stay out of this, small fry!

42
02:58.825 --> 02:59.909
That reminds me.

43
03:00.785 --> 03:02.328
I heard something about you.

44
03:02.787 --> 03:04.747
You've got a taste for Western food, haven't you?

45
03:05.999 --> 03:08.501
I've always wanted to try some.

46
03:09.377 --> 03:11.754
What was it called again?

47
03:15.133 --> 03:16.050
Tempura?

48
03:19.137 --> 03:21.681
All that searching, and still no sign of him.

49
03:23.558 --> 03:25.893
Where on earth is Sasuke?

50
03:26.561 --> 03:29.856
Maybe that monkey ran back to the mountains.

51
03:31.190 --> 03:33.860
I can't imagine him giving up on revenge.

52
03:33.943 --> 03:36.404
Who cares? Let him do as he pleases.

53
03:36.487 --> 03:38.740
Of all times for Sasuke to disappear…

54
03:41.951 --> 03:42.910
Hey…

55
03:44.996 --> 03:46.456
Have you seen Isa or Seikai?

56
03:49.751 --> 03:50.877
Mind if I ask you something?

57
03:51.753 --> 03:55.506
Can a ninja change masters?

58
03:56.924 --> 03:59.260
Well… it's not unheard of.

59
04:00.053 --> 04:01.637
-I see. -Don't write it down.

60
04:02.555 --> 04:06.309
My lord, about the name of our outpost…

61
04:06.392 --> 04:07.852
What? Now?

62
04:08.561 --> 04:10.021
You entrusted me with a great task.

63
04:10.104 --> 04:13.483
I, Mochizuki, have spent the entire night pondering it.

64
04:15.026 --> 04:16.444
Have you come up with a good name?

65
04:19.280 --> 04:21.783
How does "Sanadamaru" sound?

66
04:21.866 --> 04:22.784
That's too obvious!

67
04:23.534 --> 04:24.786
I rather like it.

68
04:25.787 --> 04:29.123
What better name to show the world the might of the Sanada?

69
04:29.707 --> 04:30.541
Yes, my lord.

70
04:34.128 --> 04:36.005
-It's one of the Toyotomi retainers. -Wait.

71
04:37.006 --> 04:38.049
There's no need to hide.

72
04:47.183 --> 04:48.810
Perhaps you weren't aware.

73
04:49.769 --> 04:53.064
Ninja are forbidden within the castle walls.

74
04:53.606 --> 04:56.192
We have Lord Hideyori's permission.

75
04:58.361 --> 05:01.531
So you've even managed to win Lord Hideyori over.

76
05:02.448 --> 05:05.284
You truly are a master of intrigue.

77
05:06.119 --> 05:07.620
I heard the news.

78
05:09.997 --> 05:12.500
Some of your retainers have deserted you.

79
05:13.668 --> 05:15.378
Come to think of it…

80
05:16.254 --> 05:19.215
Where's that cocky monkey of yours?

81
05:19.715 --> 05:21.592
That's the trouble with ninja.

82
05:22.844 --> 05:25.471
They know the castle's inner workings.

83
05:26.013 --> 05:28.182
We cannot risk them defecting to the enemy.

84
05:28.766 --> 05:31.436
I trust you'll see that they're dealt with.

85
05:32.645 --> 05:34.522
They would never betray us.

86
05:34.605 --> 05:38.151
I doubt ninja who serve for money know much of loyalty.

87
05:38.901 --> 05:40.111
You need not worry.

88
05:41.404 --> 05:44.657
We shall claim victory at the outpost.

89
05:44.740 --> 05:46.033
You have my word.

90
05:48.536 --> 05:50.830
ONO HARUNAGA

91
05:50.913 --> 05:52.415
About that…

92
05:53.457 --> 05:56.043
I've been placed in command of all our forces.

93
05:57.044 --> 05:58.254
The outpost included.

94
06:00.423 --> 06:02.049
After the recent incident,

95
06:02.592 --> 06:06.804
many have questioned whether Sanada can be trusted, given his use of ninja.

96
06:06.888 --> 06:08.806
I'm afraid I had little choice.

97
06:10.099 --> 06:11.475
From now on,

98
06:12.226 --> 06:14.604
you'll be taking your orders from me.

99
06:17.982 --> 06:19.483
SANADAMARU

100
06:21.777 --> 06:23.154
"Sanadamaru."

101
06:28.159 --> 06:30.828
You named the fortress after yourself.

102
06:30.912 --> 06:32.038
ODA URAKUSAI

103
06:32.121 --> 06:33.915
I suppose I can see why.

104
06:34.916 --> 06:36.000
But…

105
06:36.542 --> 06:39.754
you'd best live up to that name.

106
06:46.802 --> 06:49.722
I understand your desire for glory in battle,

107
06:49.805 --> 06:53.267
but this is the Toyotomi's war.

108
06:54.435 --> 06:55.978
Do not…

109
06:57.063 --> 06:58.231
forget your place.

110
07:08.908 --> 07:10.117
Fear not.

111
07:10.201 --> 07:13.371
Once we have the outpost, we'll be ready to fight at any moment.

112
07:19.335 --> 07:22.838
Aren't you going to consult your dice like you always do?

113
07:25.049 --> 07:27.426
They haven't been much help lately.

114
07:35.226 --> 07:36.936
If Sasuke were here…

115
07:38.646 --> 07:40.481
he'd have given him a piece of his mind.

116
07:55.121 --> 07:56.205
Damn, this is good!

117
07:58.916 --> 08:02.670
There's something I wish to discuss with the Ogosho.

118
08:02.753 --> 08:03.588
Well?

119
08:04.338 --> 08:06.716
Have you decided to serve me?

120
08:07.842 --> 08:09.552
I'm still pretty torn.

121
08:11.679 --> 08:15.725
By the way, why are you so bent on wiping out the Toyotomi?

122
08:17.310 --> 08:19.186
-This is good! -To bring peace to the land.

123
08:20.187 --> 08:21.355
And to do that,

124
08:21.439 --> 08:24.233
all who oppose me must be eliminated.

125
08:25.318 --> 08:28.904
Only absolute power can keep the peace.

126
08:30.823 --> 08:32.742
Well, well. Lord Hidetada.

127
08:33.743 --> 08:36.621
So this is Sanada's ninja.

128
08:39.415 --> 08:41.917
Father, allow me to kill him.

129
08:44.045 --> 08:47.673
You surely haven't forgotten what he did to me at Ueda?

130
08:47.757 --> 08:51.844
So you're the idiot son who lost to a mere thousand Sanada troops.

131
08:51.927 --> 08:53.387
Not a thousand! Two thousand!

132
08:54.680 --> 08:55.848
How dare you…

133
08:57.016 --> 08:57.850
Enough!

134
08:58.809 --> 09:01.228
The man you should be killing is Sanada Yukimura.

135
09:02.855 --> 09:04.440
You talk a big game,

136
09:05.316 --> 09:07.777
but you're just bitter about losing to Sanada, aren't you?

137
09:08.986 --> 09:10.237
Ogosho.

138
09:10.321 --> 09:15.576
I agree with Lord Hidetada. This ninja should be put to death.

139
09:16.410 --> 09:20.456
He may well become a threat to us one day.

140
09:20.539 --> 09:22.792
He is my ninja.

141
09:30.299 --> 09:32.927
Know your place, Hanzo.

142
09:33.761 --> 09:34.887
Wait!

143
09:35.805 --> 09:36.681
Another serving!

144
09:38.724 --> 09:40.685
I understand your concerns.

145
09:41.519 --> 09:44.480
But remember, you're dealing with the Ogosho himself.

146
09:45.231 --> 09:46.107
Tread carefully.

147
09:46.982 --> 09:47.817
Yes, sir.

148
09:49.193 --> 09:50.569
What of Sanada?

149
09:50.653 --> 09:52.947
He appears to be preparing for battle.

150
09:53.030 --> 09:54.365
Keep a close watch on him.

151
09:54.949 --> 09:55.825
Yes, sir.

152
09:56.951 --> 09:58.869
Once this creature awakens,

153
09:59.704 --> 10:01.706
the tide of battle will turn.

154
10:02.498 --> 10:06.669
And then, we'll have no further need for Sanada's ninja.

155
10:08.254 --> 10:10.214
How much longer do you intend to sleep?

156
10:42.246 --> 10:43.372
Hey, Saizo.

157
10:44.874 --> 10:47.960
What did Hattori Hanzo say to you back then?

158
10:53.048 --> 10:55.134
Ninja are despised

159
10:55.843 --> 10:58.637
and used as pawns by the Toyotomi, only to die in the end.

160
10:59.805 --> 11:01.015
Join the Tokugawa.

161
11:02.057 --> 11:04.560
He said the Toyotomi would use us as pawns and leave us to die.

162
11:05.644 --> 11:06.979
That it was my fate.

163
11:10.566 --> 11:11.901
He may be right.

164
11:15.613 --> 11:16.780
But…

165
11:18.199 --> 11:20.284
I have to fight all the same.

166
11:23.162 --> 11:24.163
Saizo.

167
11:27.333 --> 11:28.459
What do you fight for?

168
11:32.505 --> 11:33.672
I…

169
11:49.772 --> 11:50.689
What's this?

170
11:51.690 --> 11:54.610
Goto will defend the main bailey.

171
11:54.693 --> 11:57.238
Kimura and Chosokabe will hold Hatchome.

172
11:58.322 --> 12:00.241
Akashi, the Kizugawa approach.

173
12:00.824 --> 12:02.368
Hold your positions at all costs.

174
12:03.244 --> 12:05.412
No acting on your own!

175
12:06.288 --> 12:07.248
Understood?

176
12:07.331 --> 12:08.499
Yes, sir.

177
12:13.546 --> 12:15.923
Why must we take orders from a man who's never seen battle?

178
12:16.006 --> 12:17.091
GOTO MATABEI

179
12:17.174 --> 12:18.842
And the ronin?

180
12:20.261 --> 12:21.345
How is their morale?

181
12:23.806 --> 12:25.683
They may be a ragtag bunch,

182
12:26.350 --> 12:28.769
but I have them under control.

183
12:28.852 --> 12:30.145
You need not worry.

184
12:31.981 --> 12:33.023
And Sanada?

185
12:33.983 --> 12:38.279
He's building the outpost as ordered.

186
12:38.946 --> 12:40.573
Everything is proceeding smoothly.

187
12:45.536 --> 12:46.745
Just a little more!

188
12:51.208 --> 12:52.042
Good work.

189
12:52.126 --> 12:55.129
Ono seems to be struggling to keep the ronin in line.

190
12:55.796 --> 12:56.797
Hardly surprising.

191
12:57.590 --> 13:00.050
He may be skilled in castle politics,

192
13:00.134 --> 13:02.344
but he has never fought a battle.

193
13:03.095 --> 13:06.348
How could he possibly command the ronin?

194
13:07.308 --> 13:09.893
At this rate, we'll lose a war we could've won.

195
13:11.061 --> 13:13.439
We must focus on what we can do.

196
13:15.107 --> 13:17.026
Good work, everyone.

197
13:17.109 --> 13:19.862
Lord Yukimura! It's been so long!

198
13:19.945 --> 13:21.030
Okuni.

199
13:21.113 --> 13:23.115
So you're all together.

200
13:23.198 --> 13:24.783
I'm glad you're safe.

201
13:24.867 --> 13:27.620
I heard your village was burned down. What happened to the others?

202
13:28.412 --> 13:29.496
I don't know.

203
13:30.080 --> 13:31.665
I just ran for my life…

204
13:32.499 --> 13:34.668
You escaped the village alone?

205
13:37.338 --> 13:40.841
I was so scared… I'm sorry.

206
13:41.508 --> 13:44.428
No, it's all right. Forgive me.

207
13:46.138 --> 13:47.431
So that's how you ended up here?

208
13:47.973 --> 13:51.769
I was fortunate enough to be taken in. I work here at the castle now.

209
13:52.811 --> 13:53.979
If you'll excuse me.

210
13:55.731 --> 13:58.484
-Please, everyone, help yourselves. -Lord Yukimura.

211
14:17.795 --> 14:18.879
Look at this.

212
14:22.633 --> 14:24.843
This is Sasuke's Muramasa sword…

213
14:26.053 --> 14:29.765
A townsman claimed he'd seen someone resembling Sasuke.

214
14:29.848 --> 14:32.101
We searched the area, and found this nearby.

215
14:33.018 --> 14:35.312
Something may have happened to Sasuke.

216
14:36.647 --> 14:39.149
The Tokugawa may have captured him.

217
14:40.234 --> 14:41.276
What makes you think that?

218
14:43.404 --> 14:44.363
Saizo…

219
14:45.322 --> 14:46.657
encountered Hanzo.

220
14:48.117 --> 14:49.868
But Hanzo made no attempt to kill him.

221
14:51.453 --> 14:54.248
It's possible. He may have wanted to use him.

222
14:56.333 --> 14:58.460
Judging by what happened to Lady Okurakyo…

223
15:01.588 --> 15:05.009
the Tokugawa may have a ninja who can control minds.

224
15:06.218 --> 15:08.804
You think they're trying to turn Sasuke against us?

225
15:13.100 --> 15:14.226
Saizo, a word.

226
15:15.227 --> 15:16.103
Yes, my lord.

227
15:20.315 --> 15:24.111
Once the battle begins, the enemy's defenses should weaken.

228
15:25.779 --> 15:28.741
I want you to use that chance to rescue Sasuke.

229
15:32.369 --> 15:33.954
It will be a dangerous mission.

230
15:34.663 --> 15:35.789
Can I count on you?

231
15:50.596 --> 15:52.723
I am Urano Motokuni.

232
15:54.391 --> 15:57.936
His family has been related to ours since my grandfather's time.

233
15:58.020 --> 16:00.898
He's our most trusted samurai.

234
16:01.607 --> 16:04.610
I can't leave the outpost in Sanada's hands alone,

235
16:05.319 --> 16:08.113
so he'll be stationed there as well.

236
16:08.197 --> 16:10.032
That is most reassuring.

237
16:10.866 --> 16:12.076
I'm counting on you.

238
16:12.159 --> 16:12.993
Yes, my lady.

239
16:13.077 --> 16:15.496
I've brought my finest men.

240
16:17.081 --> 16:20.334
We'll defend the outpost with our lives.

241
16:39.895 --> 16:43.607
So even tempura wasn't enough to win him over.

242
16:44.858 --> 16:49.029
I even threw in an extra-large shrimp. You rarely come across one of those.

243
16:52.157 --> 16:53.992
That should make him cooperate.

244
16:55.202 --> 16:56.120
Now…

245
16:57.663 --> 16:59.998
write, Sasuke.

246
17:01.959 --> 17:04.169
Write down everything you've seen.

247
17:07.339 --> 17:08.257
Yes.

248
17:38.036 --> 17:39.079
Well done.

249
17:41.498 --> 17:42.332
Here.

250
17:52.467 --> 17:54.344
What did Lord Yukimura ask you to do?

251
17:55.429 --> 17:56.722
Is it about Sasuke?

252
18:02.394 --> 18:03.228
Yuri.

253
18:04.479 --> 18:05.814
Remember what we talked about?

254
18:08.150 --> 18:10.736
What we'd do when this war's over?

255
18:17.451 --> 18:20.746
If I make it back alive, there's something I want to tell you.

256
18:51.526 --> 18:53.946
Are you ready for battle?

257
18:54.613 --> 18:55.447
Yes, sir!

258
18:55.530 --> 18:59.117
We'll defend this outpost at all costs!

259
18:59.201 --> 19:00.994
Ei! Ei! Oh!

260
19:01.078 --> 19:03.455
Ei! Ei! Oh!

261
19:03.538 --> 19:05.082
Ei! Ei! Oh!

262
19:05.707 --> 19:07.709
Ei! Ei! Oh!

263
19:10.420 --> 19:12.297
I am Urano Motokuni.

264
19:13.799 --> 19:15.842
It is an honor to fight

265
19:15.926 --> 19:19.680
alongside the man who twice defeated Lord Ieyasu.

266
19:20.639 --> 19:23.183
I'm grateful for your support.

267
19:23.267 --> 19:25.769
Urano comes from a distinguished family.

268
19:26.478 --> 19:29.606
Unlike the ninja, he's a man you can trust.

269
19:30.190 --> 19:34.152
Now, if you'll excuse me, I have preparations to make.

270
19:40.367 --> 19:43.662
Will the Ogosho truly take me into his service?

271
19:47.958 --> 19:49.876
You have the Ogosho's word.

272
19:50.836 --> 19:52.170
There's no doubt about it.

273
19:53.088 --> 19:54.172
See that you don't fail.

274
19:54.715 --> 19:56.049
I know what I'm doing.

275
20:02.973 --> 20:04.349
On the day of battle,

276
20:05.350 --> 20:08.312
my men will stage a revolt inside the outpost…

277
20:08.895 --> 20:10.439
Then send up a smoke signal.

278
20:10.522 --> 20:11.481
I see.

279
20:11.898 --> 20:13.817
Once we see that signal, we'll attack.

280
20:13.900 --> 20:16.278
We'll have them trapped from within and without.

281
20:17.237 --> 20:19.323
The outpost will fall in no time.

282
20:20.115 --> 20:23.702
Their greatest hope for victory will be the first to fall.

283
20:24.453 --> 20:25.954
How pitiful.

284
20:26.913 --> 20:30.417
I can barely contain my excitement at the thought of killing Sanada.

285
20:32.252 --> 20:33.378
Father.

286
20:33.462 --> 20:35.839
Please allow me to lead the vanguard!

287
20:35.922 --> 20:37.466
SHUN THIS WORLD, SEEK THE PURE LAND

288
20:37.549 --> 20:38.550
Hidetada.

289
20:40.052 --> 20:41.720
How do we count shrimp?

290
20:42.804 --> 20:43.764
By their tails.

291
20:43.847 --> 20:44.681
Indeed.

292
20:46.099 --> 20:46.933
And birds?

293
20:47.851 --> 20:48.769
By their feathers.

294
20:49.353 --> 20:50.645
We count living creatures

295
20:51.355 --> 20:53.357
by what they leave behind in death.

296
20:54.900 --> 20:56.568
Then what of men?

297
20:57.819 --> 20:58.695
By their names.

298
21:00.280 --> 21:02.449
A man's name is what lives on.

299
21:03.909 --> 21:05.911
Redeem yourself in this battle.

300
21:06.912 --> 21:08.830
Make a name for yourself, Hidetada.

301
21:09.539 --> 21:10.540
Yes, Father!

302
21:14.836 --> 21:16.421
Make way, everyone!

303
21:18.048 --> 21:20.342
Her Ladyship has come to encourage the troops.

304
21:23.220 --> 21:24.096
All of you,

305
21:24.805 --> 21:26.598
fight to your last breath.

306
21:28.141 --> 21:30.435
You must defend the Toyotomi!

307
21:30.519 --> 21:31.645
Yes, my lady.

308
21:31.728 --> 21:34.272
What does she think our lives are worth?

309
21:35.816 --> 21:37.025
I'm counting on you.

310
21:37.109 --> 21:38.318
Yes, my lady…

311
21:46.201 --> 21:49.413
That should raise the ronin's spirits.

312
21:49.496 --> 21:50.455
Indeed.

313
21:50.539 --> 21:52.541
We are most grateful for your kindness.

314
21:52.624 --> 21:55.210
Victory is all but assured.

315
22:06.763 --> 22:08.098
The time has finally come.

316
22:09.099 --> 22:10.600
Fourteen years in Kudoyama…

317
22:11.560 --> 22:13.103
All for this day.

318
22:23.155 --> 22:25.448
I've kept you all waiting long enough.

319
22:39.963 --> 22:41.047
Let's do this.

320
22:55.437 --> 22:57.189
A smoke signal from the outpost!

321
23:01.276 --> 23:03.153
Good.

322
23:05.614 --> 23:06.489
What's happening?

323
23:12.871 --> 23:14.539
Urgent news!

324
23:15.790 --> 23:17.584
-We've got trouble! -What is it?

325
23:17.667 --> 23:19.502
There's a revolt inside the outpost!

326
23:20.462 --> 23:21.421
Then…

327
23:22.005 --> 23:23.215
that smoke signal is…

328
23:24.132 --> 23:27.469
It must be… a signal to the Tokugawa.

329
23:28.553 --> 23:29.971
What does this mean?

330
23:30.055 --> 23:32.515
What is going on? Harunaga!

331
23:33.099 --> 23:34.684
Yes, my lady! Excuse me!

332
23:43.568 --> 23:45.612
Well then, shall we begin?

333
23:48.365 --> 23:50.116
Our first battle since Sekigahara.

334
23:55.038 --> 23:56.831
Bring them forward!

335
24:01.962 --> 24:03.463
I'll avenge my humiliation

336
24:04.506 --> 24:05.757
at Ueda.

337
24:08.635 --> 24:11.513
Just watch me, Father.

338
24:15.225 --> 24:17.477
By the authority of the Shogun, I command you!

339
24:18.645 --> 24:20.438
Charge!

340
24:54.139 --> 24:55.015
Suden.

341
24:55.890 --> 24:56.933
What's happening?

342
24:57.017 --> 24:59.894
There appears to be no sign of a revolt.

343
24:59.978 --> 25:01.855
Our forces are facing fierce resistance.

344
25:03.815 --> 25:06.318
Then what was that smoke signal?

345
25:09.738 --> 25:10.947
Don't tell me…

346
25:13.033 --> 25:15.160
The enemy's falling one after another…

347
25:15.243 --> 25:16.202
What of the revolt?

348
25:17.078 --> 25:18.204
What's happened to it?

349
25:18.788 --> 25:19.873
The revolt…

350
25:20.790 --> 25:21.916
What happened to it?

351
25:22.000 --> 25:22.834
Revolt?

352
25:23.460 --> 25:24.669
Whatever do you mean?

353
25:24.753 --> 25:27.005
The enemy sent up a smoke signal!

354
25:27.088 --> 25:28.131
And their banners fell!

355
25:28.214 --> 25:29.924
Forgive me for keeping you in the dark.

356
25:31.426 --> 25:33.219
The fallen banners were a ruse.

357
25:34.012 --> 25:37.182
And the smoke signal was a trap to lure the enemy in.

358
25:38.183 --> 25:40.518
We stopped the revolt before it could begin.

359
25:41.811 --> 25:45.440
I suspected the enemy was plotting to turn our men against us.

360
25:45.523 --> 25:47.067
So I took precautions.

361
25:48.234 --> 25:49.194
Precautions?

362
25:49.277 --> 25:53.573
I planted a trusted retainer among the men stationed at the outpost.

363
25:58.203 --> 25:59.871
This is the man who led the plot.

364
25:59.954 --> 26:01.206
Urano!

365
26:01.873 --> 26:04.250
Well done, Isa, Seikai.

366
26:05.293 --> 26:06.294
Yes, my lord!

367
26:06.378 --> 26:09.798
This is the Toyotomi's war.

368
26:11.007 --> 26:12.592
Do not…

369
26:13.718 --> 26:14.719
forget your place.

370
26:19.224 --> 26:21.017
We're back.

371
26:22.060 --> 26:24.145
There were Tokugawa soldiers everywhere.

372
26:24.229 --> 26:26.856
You two… I thought you'd left us.

373
26:26.940 --> 26:28.691
Of course not.

374
26:28.775 --> 26:31.820
-We were just a little late getting back. -I figured as much.

375
26:34.906 --> 26:37.283
That's it. Isa, Seikai.

376
26:38.118 --> 26:40.703
Let's let everyone think you've deserted.

377
26:43.289 --> 26:45.041
Ei! Ei! Oh!

378
26:45.625 --> 26:47.585
Ei! Ei! Oh!

379
26:49.170 --> 26:50.004
Thanks to them,

380
26:50.547 --> 26:52.841
we learned of the Tokugawa's plot ahead of time.

381
26:53.758 --> 26:54.759
Urano…

382
26:56.511 --> 26:57.887
why would you do this?

383
27:04.394 --> 27:07.272
Even if you win this battle,

384
27:08.940 --> 27:11.276
the Toyotomi clan has no future!

385
28:51.543 --> 28:52.752
Impressive…

386
28:54.087 --> 28:55.171
A man's worth

387
28:55.922 --> 28:58.550
isn't determined solely by his bloodline or family name.

388
29:01.052 --> 29:04.222
I suggest you stop underestimating my Ten Braves.

389
29:07.475 --> 29:09.811
Raise the banners!

390
29:14.649 --> 29:18.611
Look! The Sanada banners are flying!

391
29:21.447 --> 29:23.241
Follow Sanada!

392
29:23.324 --> 29:24.993
Drive the enemy back!

393
29:30.498 --> 29:33.209
The Sanada banners have united the men…

394
29:34.752 --> 29:36.671
It seems my words have inspired them.

395
29:48.057 --> 29:49.392
Damn you, Sanada!

396
29:50.268 --> 29:51.352
How dare you!

397
29:52.228 --> 29:54.689
Hold this position at all costs!

398
30:05.617 --> 30:07.118
Our men are driving them back.

399
30:10.580 --> 30:12.415
The rest is up to you, Saizo.

400
30:14.375 --> 30:16.044
We're ready to withdraw.

401
30:22.133 --> 30:22.967
Father!

402
30:23.051 --> 30:26.304
The enemy was waiting for us. It seems they knew our plan.

403
30:26.387 --> 30:28.181
Silence! Silence! Silence!

404
30:29.265 --> 30:30.975
You let yourself be outwitted!

405
30:31.851 --> 30:33.561
You fool!

406
30:36.731 --> 30:38.024
Hey!

407
30:38.107 --> 30:39.859
The Ogosho is returning.

408
30:39.943 --> 30:40.985
TAISEIJI TEMPLE

409
31:15.103 --> 31:16.020
Did you hear?

410
31:16.104 --> 31:18.439
Apparently, some strange creature is locked in the dungeon.

411
31:18.523 --> 31:20.149
I'd rather not go anywhere near it.

412
31:20.233 --> 31:21.067
Nor would I.

413
31:39.544 --> 31:40.378
Sasuke!

414
31:41.254 --> 31:42.213
Can you move?

415
31:43.172 --> 31:44.132
Get a hold of yourself!

416
31:54.934 --> 31:55.768
Hey.

417
31:59.731 --> 32:02.400
Here. I brought this for you.

418
32:14.662 --> 32:15.705
Kill him.

419
32:16.497 --> 32:18.041
He is the enemy.

420
32:23.129 --> 32:24.130
Yes.

421
32:31.971 --> 32:35.266
Since when did a monkey like you start taking orders?

422
32:52.700 --> 32:53.534
Hey!

423
33:17.850 --> 33:19.102
Snap out of it.

424
33:20.353 --> 33:21.229
Sasuke.

425
33:23.231 --> 33:24.273
Sasuke!

426
33:41.040 --> 33:42.083
Sasuke.

427
33:42.750 --> 33:44.377
Kill him.

428
33:45.128 --> 33:46.045
Kill him!

429
33:49.590 --> 33:50.967
Shut the hell up, you old hag!

430
33:57.765 --> 33:59.725
I'm one of the Sanada Ten Braves.

431
34:01.477 --> 34:03.271
Sarutobi Sasuke.

432
34:05.565 --> 34:08.192
And I hate being told what to do!

433
34:08.818 --> 34:10.444
He broke my spell…

434
34:11.279 --> 34:12.446
through sheer willpower?

435
34:13.030 --> 34:13.990
You stupid monkey.

436
34:14.782 --> 34:16.576
You've finally come to your senses?

437
34:16.659 --> 34:19.912
Why'd you come for me? I walked out on you.

438
34:20.997 --> 34:22.540
You really think Lord Yukimura

439
34:23.416 --> 34:24.500
would abandon you?

440
34:26.919 --> 34:28.212
Kill them!

441
34:31.382 --> 34:32.550
Damn it…

442
34:33.843 --> 34:34.719
Let's go.

443
34:38.848 --> 34:40.224
What the hell is that?

444
34:40.808 --> 34:42.351
That's one ugly bird.

445
34:55.406 --> 34:56.908
-Ieyasu! -Wait!

446
35:45.915 --> 35:48.000
I should've killed you after all.

447
35:50.294 --> 35:51.254
Hey, Saizo.

448
35:51.963 --> 35:53.089
Let's do that move.

449
35:54.590 --> 35:55.925
The Saizo Special?

450
35:56.759 --> 35:58.636
It's the Sasuke Special!

451
36:09.397 --> 36:10.273
Switch!

452
36:10.356 --> 36:11.607
SWITCH

453
36:16.320 --> 36:17.363
Saizo!

454
36:33.838 --> 36:35.715
You bastard!

455
36:39.176 --> 36:40.303
Sasuke…

456
36:44.265 --> 36:45.683
You're strong.

457
36:47.768 --> 36:49.103
Far stronger than I am.

458
36:50.730 --> 36:51.605
And you…

459
36:53.941 --> 36:55.276
You have a place to go home to!

460
37:05.494 --> 37:07.288
Take care of Lord Yukimura…

461
37:09.081 --> 37:10.249
You stupid monkey.

462
38:15.314 --> 38:16.440
Seikai, get down!

463
38:21.362 --> 38:23.322
Seikai, don't push yourself too hard.

464
38:24.073 --> 38:24.907
Yeah.

465
38:27.952 --> 38:29.662
The enemy is retreating!

466
38:31.163 --> 38:33.165
The first battle is ours.

467
38:33.958 --> 38:34.792
Indeed.

468
38:39.964 --> 38:42.299
-You've all fought valiantly! -Yes, sir!

469
38:42.383 --> 38:44.802
-Victory belongs to the Toyotomi! -Yes, sir!

470
38:51.183 --> 38:53.644
AS OUR FORCES HAVE ALSO SUFFERED LOSSES,

471
38:53.727 --> 38:55.980
I BELIEVE WE SHOULD SEEK PEACE.

472
38:58.691 --> 38:59.692
Peace?

473
39:04.321 --> 39:05.489
Father,

474
39:05.573 --> 39:08.826
we may have withdrawn, but we haven't lost.

475
39:08.909 --> 39:10.703
Isn't it too soon to seek peace?

476
39:10.786 --> 39:12.538
If we keep fighting, sooner or later…

477
39:13.414 --> 39:14.957
Sooner or later, we'll win.

478
39:16.083 --> 39:17.626
And that is precisely the problem.

479
39:19.086 --> 39:22.381
If word spreads that even Hideyori can give me trouble,

480
39:23.090 --> 39:24.967
my reputation will suffer.

481
39:25.050 --> 39:27.887
-But if the Toyotomi bloodline survives-- -Hidetada.

482
39:30.931 --> 39:32.933
Who said anything about letting them live?

483
39:34.935 --> 39:35.895
Ogosho!

484
39:37.980 --> 39:38.981
It's…

485
39:40.858 --> 39:42.193
finally awakened!

486
39:44.528 --> 39:45.571
Is that true?

487
39:49.783 --> 39:51.118
Wonderful news!

488
39:53.871 --> 39:56.373
You've all done splendidly.

489
39:56.457 --> 39:59.710
That's three victories over the Tokugawa, my lord!

490
39:59.793 --> 40:01.462
Yes!

491
40:01.545 --> 40:02.922
It's all thanks to you two.

492
40:03.672 --> 40:05.466
Well done infiltrating their ranks.

493
40:06.592 --> 40:08.219
A fine job, Miyoshi brothers.

494
40:09.512 --> 40:10.471
Glad it all worked out.

495
40:10.554 --> 40:11.430
Yeah.

496
40:11.514 --> 40:13.098
That armor looks good on you.

497
40:13.182 --> 40:14.433
Pardon the interruption.

498
40:15.351 --> 40:19.313
Lord Ono, Lord Sanada. Lady Yodo requests your presence.

499
40:24.818 --> 40:26.403
Think we're getting a reward?

500
40:27.238 --> 40:28.489
Now that would be nice.

501
40:31.617 --> 40:32.826
Peace?

502
40:32.910 --> 40:35.371
The offer came from the Tokugawa side.

503
40:36.080 --> 40:38.207
All thanks to your valiant efforts.

504
40:39.917 --> 40:41.835
We mustn't trust Ieyasu.

505
40:41.919 --> 40:43.420
He must have something up his sleeve.

506
40:44.171 --> 40:45.422
It could be a trap.

507
40:46.715 --> 40:50.386
Our victory has shown him what we're capable of.

508
40:51.095 --> 40:52.638
You're worrying too much.

509
40:54.848 --> 40:56.809
Peace is exactly what we want.

510
40:57.518 --> 40:58.894
This will put an end to the war.

511
40:59.395 --> 41:00.563
What more could we ask?

512
41:01.188 --> 41:03.607
I've had quite enough of war.

513
41:05.317 --> 41:07.027
Surely you agree, Yukimura?

514
41:08.362 --> 41:10.781
Then allow me to send my ninja

515
41:11.532 --> 41:13.409
to uncover Ieyasu's true intentions.

516
41:13.492 --> 41:15.077
Ninja, huh?

517
41:15.703 --> 41:16.954
They cannot be trusted.

518
41:18.080 --> 41:19.999
Wouldn't you agree, Lord Ono?

519
41:21.792 --> 41:22.960
I believe…

520
41:25.421 --> 41:27.840
we should leave this matter to Sanada.

521
41:29.091 --> 41:29.925
What?

522
41:30.009 --> 41:30.843
Harunaga?

523
41:31.969 --> 41:35.514
We owe our victory to that outpost…

524
41:36.307 --> 41:39.018
No, to Sanadamaru

525
41:39.643 --> 41:42.229
and the efforts of Sanada's ninja.

526
41:43.188 --> 41:44.106
Lord Ono…

527
41:46.650 --> 41:47.735
We should put our faith…

528
41:49.403 --> 41:50.362
in them.

529
41:54.116 --> 41:55.159
Very well.

530
41:56.869 --> 41:58.454
If Harunaga says so,

531
42:00.247 --> 42:02.541
we shall determine the Tokugawa's intentions

532
42:03.167 --> 42:04.460
before agreeing to peace.

533
42:04.543 --> 42:06.754
But surely, Lady Yodo…

534
42:15.846 --> 42:16.847
Sasuke!

535
42:17.556 --> 42:20.017
You're alive! Thank goodness!

536
42:20.100 --> 42:24.355
Where the hell have you been? You had us worried!

537
42:24.438 --> 42:25.981
The Tokugawa captured me.

538
42:26.065 --> 42:27.775
How'd you manage to escape?

539
42:28.484 --> 42:30.361
Saizo came to my rescue.

540
42:30.444 --> 42:34.156
I knew the bonds of the Sanada could never be broken.

541
42:34.239 --> 42:35.491
But…

542
42:35.574 --> 42:36.492
Where's Saizo?

543
42:45.376 --> 42:46.460
Sasuke.

544
42:50.464 --> 42:51.548
Where is Saizo?

545
42:56.261 --> 42:57.388
Where is he?

546
43:06.689 --> 43:07.564
I'm sorry.

547
43:12.820 --> 43:14.279
Saizo's dead.

548
43:22.621 --> 43:23.747
It's my fault…

549
43:27.042 --> 43:28.711
He gave his life to save mine…

550
44:08.459 --> 44:11.628
-What's happening? -I don't know!

551
44:11.712 --> 44:12.838
It just came out of nowhere!

552
44:15.466 --> 44:16.508
Everyone!

553
44:17.217 --> 44:19.553
Lady Yodo! Please, get back!

554
44:19.636 --> 44:21.847
-Stay away! -Please, stand back!

555
44:21.930 --> 44:23.390
Hey, you saw that, right?

556
44:23.474 --> 44:25.934
Something flying overhead dropped a bomb.

557
44:26.435 --> 44:28.061
What the hell was that thing?

558
44:28.145 --> 44:31.231
Wait, isn't that Lady Yodo's bedchamber?

559
44:31.815 --> 44:32.983
You don't think…

560
44:33.066 --> 44:34.902
She was the target?

561
44:36.612 --> 44:37.696
Write.

562
44:37.780 --> 44:39.782
Write down everything you've seen.

563
44:44.453 --> 44:45.829
Enough!

564
44:48.248 --> 44:49.833
The war is over!

565
44:51.543 --> 44:52.628
We shall make peace.

566
44:53.212 --> 44:55.297
Make peace at once!

567
45:00.969 --> 45:02.221
A fine fit indeed.

568
45:02.304 --> 45:04.473
Or perhaps this one? What about this?

569
45:05.140 --> 45:07.768
This is rather splendid too. How am I to choose?

570
45:07.851 --> 45:12.022
Surely no ninja alive could leap higher than this one.

571
45:12.814 --> 45:13.899
Magnificent.

572
45:14.525 --> 45:16.610
Truly magnificent, Suden.

573
45:17.778 --> 45:18.946
You honor me, my lord.

574
45:20.030 --> 45:22.574
At last, the ninja we've sought for so long.

575
45:23.158 --> 45:24.493
One who transcends human limits…

576
45:24.993 --> 45:27.079
Unrivaled under heaven.

577
45:28.622 --> 45:33.126
And you, on the other hand… You let Sasuke escape.

578
45:34.711 --> 45:35.546
You fool.

579
45:44.513 --> 45:46.348
-Is anybody there? -Lord Yukimura!

580
45:50.561 --> 45:51.395
Someone…

581
46:26.179 --> 46:31.184
Subtitle translation by: Sayo Takada

582
46:31.268 --> 46:33.186
THIS DRAMA IS A WORK OF FICTION
